# roam-332: never hang-watch a BACKGROUND thread-pool worker, even during shutdown.
#
# Backport of ONE line from upstream ebcfffbb36aca8c977ecc3355786eda8a0315a72
# (M152). WorkerThread::RunWorker decides whether to register the new thread with
# the HangWatcher; at this pin it asks GetDesiredThreadType(), which is NOT the
# thread's immutable hint:
#
#   ThreadType WorkerThread::GetDesiredThreadType() const {
#     // To avoid shutdown hangs, disallow a type below kNormal during shutdown
#     if (task_tracker_->HasShutdownStarted())
#       return ThreadType::kDefault;
#     return thread_type_hint_;
#   }
#
# So once shutdown has started, a BACKGROUND worker reports kDefault and is
# treated as watchable — losing the exemption the comment above the gate says it
# should have. HangWatcher::RegisterThreadInternal then runs
# CHECK(base::FeatureList::GetInstance()) (base/threading/hang_watcher.cc:784),
# and in a browser test the framework has torn the FeatureList down by then
# (ScopedFeatureList::Reset clears unconditionally before restoring, and
# FeatureListScopedToEachTest resets after the fixture is destroyed). The worker
# aborts the process AFTER the test body passed, which the launcher records as
# FAILURE_ON_EXIT — the roam-332 flake family (two observations, 2026-09-08,
# RoamuxRefreshAllInitialUrlsTest and RoamuxNewTabPositionTest; the crash stack
# is RunBackgroundSharedWorker -> RunWorker -> RegisterThreadInternal).
#
# Upstream's fix is to read the immutable hint. That closes the observed path
# exactly: RunBackgroundSharedWorker is only reachable under
# `if (thread_type_hint_ == ThreadType::kBackground)` (worker_thread.cc:315), so
# the hint gate excludes precisely those workers, no matter which FeatureList
# reset is the operative one — which this change therefore does not need to
# determine.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX: a NON-background worker registering while the
# FeatureList is null. The CHECK outlives the state it guards —
# IsThreadPoolHangWatchingEnabled() reads a cached atomic stored once at init
# (hang_watcher.cc:515-517, :573-576) — so the general lifetime hazard remains,
# upstream and here. Nothing observed has hit it.
#
# RETIREMENT (roam-293 / roam-291): at every uprev, check whether the pinned
# worker_thread.cc already gates on thread_type_hint_. When it does, DELETE this
# patch — it is upstream's own change, carried early. apply_patches failing on
# changed context here is that signal arriving on its own.
#
# The code change is byte-identical to upstream's so retirement is unambiguous;
# all Roamux reasoning lives in this preamble, not in the diff.
#
# NO REGRESSION TEST — an accepted trade-off, not an impossibility. The
# registration decision itself is observable
# (HangWatchState::GetHangWatchStateForCurrentThread(), and base's worker-test
# delegates allow controlled shutdown ordering with a live FeatureList);
# reproducing the original crash additionally needs a null FeatureList in a live
# process and produces an abort rather than a failing assertion. Testing the
# decision would take base internals or a patch-carried test (roam-282 moved this
# repo away from those), so acceptance here is the verified mechanism plus green
# suites. SHIPPED-BUILD EFFECT: this is production base/ code, not test-only —
# background-hinted workers reaching the gate after shutdown starts no longer
# register or take hang-watch scopes. Scheduling priority promotion is unchanged
# and non-background monitoring is untouched; the change restores the exemption
# the comment directly above the gate already states, and matches upstream.
diff --git a/base/task/thread_pool/worker_thread.cc b/base/task/thread_pool/worker_thread.cc
index fef42104f6..47b22b8448 100644
--- a/base/task/thread_pool/worker_thread.cc
+++ b/base/task/thread_pool/worker_thread.cc
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@ void WorkerThread::RunWorker() {
   // watch them for hangs. Ignore priority boosting for now.
   const bool watch_for_hangs =
       base::HangWatcher::IsThreadPoolHangWatchingEnabled() &&
-      GetDesiredThreadType() != ThreadType::kBackground;
+      thread_type_hint_ != ThreadType::kBackground;
 
   // If this process has a HangWatcher register this thread for watching.
   base::ScopedClosureRunner unregister_for_hang_watching;
